  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is i?', 'The imaginary unit, defined by i² = −1.', 1),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is a complex number?', 'A number of the form z = a + bi, where a and b are real.', 2),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What are Re(z) and Im(z) for z = 3 − 4i?', 'Re(z) = 3 and Im(z) = −4.', 3),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is the complex conjugate of z = a + bi?', 'z* = a − bi.', 4),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Simplify i³ and i⁴.', 'i³ = −i and i⁴ = 1.', 5),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Add (2 + 3i) + (4 − i).', '6 + 2i.', 6),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Multiply (2 + 3i)(1 − i).', '2 − 2i + 3i − 3i² = 5 + i.', 7),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is z z* for z = a + bi?', 'a² + b², which is always real and non-negative.', 8),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'How do you divide complex numbers?', 'Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator.', 9),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Calculate (3 + i)/(1 − i).', '(3 + i)(1 + i)/2 = (3 + 4i + i²)/2 = (2 + 4i)/2 = 1 + 2i.', 10),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Solve z² + 4 = 0.', 'z = ±2i.', 11),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Solve z² − 2z + 5 = 0.', 'z = (2 ± √(4 − 20))/2 = 1 ± 2i.', 12),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is an Argand diagram?', 'A diagram representing complex numbers as points, with the real part on the horizontal axis and the imaginary part on the vertical axis.', 13),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'How is z* shown on an Argand diagram?', 'As the reflection of z in the real axis.', 14),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What does |z − a| represent?', 'The distance from z to the point a on the Argand diagram.', 15),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Describe the locus |z − 2 − i| = 3.', 'A circle with centre (2, 1) and radius 3.', 16),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Describe the locus |z − 1| = |z + i|.', 'The perpendicular bisector of the points 1 and −i.', 17),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Describe the locus arg(z − 1) = π/4.', 'A half-line from (1, 0) at angle π/4 to the positive real axis, not including the point 1.', 18),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What does |z| < 2 represent?', 'The interior of a circle centred at the origin with radius 2.', 19),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Describe the region |z − 3| ≤ |z + 1|.', 'The points closer to 3 than to −1: Re(z) ≥ 1.', 20),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What does arg z = θ represent?', 'A half-line from the origin at angle θ.', 21),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is Euler''s formula?', 'e^(iθ) = cos θ + i sin θ.', 22),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is the exponential form of a complex number?', 'z = re^(iθ).', 23),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is e^(iπ)?', '−1.', 24),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'State de Moivre''s theorem.', '[r(cos θ + i sin θ)]ⁿ = rⁿ(cos nθ + i sin nθ).', 25),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Calculate (1 + i)⁸ using de Moivre.', '(√2)⁸(cos 2π + i sin 2π) = 16.', 26),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'How can de Moivre express cos 3θ in terms of cos θ?', 'Expand (cos θ + i sin θ)³ and take the real part: cos 3θ = 4cos³θ − 3cos θ.', 27),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'Express sin 3θ in terms of sin θ.', 'sin 3θ = 3 sin θ − 4 sin³θ.', 28),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is z + 1/z if z = e^(iθ)?', '2 cos θ.', 29),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Complex Numbers', 'What is z − 1/z if z = e^(iθ)?', '2i sin θ.', 30),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the order of a matrix?', 'The number of rows × the number of columns.', 1),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'When can two matrices be multiplied?', 'When the number of columns in the first equals the number of rows in the second.', 2),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'Is matrix multiplication commutative?', 'No; in general AB ≠ BA.', 3),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'Is matrix multiplication associative?', 'Yes: (AB)C = A(BC).', 4),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the identity matrix I?', 'A square matrix with 1s on the leading diagonal and 0s elsewhere; AI = IA = A.', 5),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the determinant of a 2×2 matrix (a b; c d)?', 'ad − bc.', 6),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the inverse of a 2×2 matrix (a b; c d)?', '(1/(ad − bc)) × (d −b; −c a).', 7),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is a singular matrix?', 'A matrix with determinant zero, which has no inverse.', 8),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is (AB)⁻¹?', 'B⁻¹A⁻¹.', 9),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the determinant of a 3×3 matrix?', 'Expand along a row or column using cofactors: a(ei − fh) − b(di − fg) + c(dh − eg).', 10),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What does the determinant of a transformation matrix represent?', 'The area (2D) or volume (3D) scale factor; a negative value means orientation is reversed.', 11),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How can matrices solve simultaneous equations?', 'Write as AX = B, then X = A⁻¹B if A is non-singular.', 12),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What does det A = 0 mean for a system of 3 equations?', 'There is no unique solution: either no solutions (inconsistent) or infinitely many.', 13),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do three planes with no unique solution appear geometrically?', 'As a sheaf (common line), a prism (no common point), or with parallel planes.', 14),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is det(AB)?', 'det A × det B.', 15),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the transpose of a matrix?', 'The matrix formed by swapping rows and columns, Aᵀ.', 16),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the inverse of a 3×3 matrix?', 'Find the matrix of cofactors, transpose it (adjugate), then divide by the determinant.', 17),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the zero matrix?', 'A matrix in which every element is 0.', 18),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What transformation does (1 0; 0 −1) represent?', 'A reflection in the x-axis.', 19),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What transformation does (−1 0; 0 1) represent?', 'A reflection in the y-axis.', 20),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What transformation does (0 1; 1 0) represent?', 'A reflection in the line y = x.', 21),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What matrix represents an anticlockwise rotation by θ about the origin?', '(cos θ −sin θ; sin θ cos θ).', 22),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What matrix represents an enlargement by scale factor k about the origin?', '(k 0; 0 k).', 23),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What matrix represents a stretch parallel to the x-axis, scale factor k?', '(k 0; 0 1).', 24),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What does the matrix (1 k; 0 1) represent?', 'A shear with the x-axis invariant: each point moves parallel to the x-axis by k times its y-coordinate.', 25),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the image of a point under a transformation?', 'Multiply the transformation matrix by the position vector of the point.', 26),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the matrix of a transformation?', 'Find the images of the unit vectors i and j (and k); these form the columns.', 27),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the matrix for a combined transformation "A then B"?', 'BA (the first transformation is on the right).', 28),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is an invariant point?', 'A point that maps to itself under a transformation.', 29),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is an invariant line?', 'A line where every point on it maps to a point on the same line.', 30),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is a rational function?', 'A function of the form f(x) = p(x)/q(x) where p and q are polynomials.', 1),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you find vertical asymptotes of y = p(x)/q(x)?', 'Solve q(x) = 0 (where p(x) ≠ 0).', 2),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you find the horizontal asymptote of y = (ax + b)/(cx + d)?', 'y = a/c.', 3),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the oblique asymptote of y = (x² + 1)/x?', 'y = x, since y = x + 1/x.', 4),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How can you find the range of y = (x² + 1)/(x − 1)?', 'Rearrange into a quadratic in x and use the discriminant ≥ 0 for real x.', 5),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is y = 1/f(x) used for?', 'Sketching the reciprocal graph: roots of f become vertical asymptotes, and maxima become minima.', 6),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How is y = |f(x)| sketched?', 'Reflect the parts of y = f(x) below the x-axis in the x-axis.', 7),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How is y² = f(x) sketched?', 'Plot y = ±√f(x) where f(x) ≥ 0; the graph is symmetric about the x-axis.', 8),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Solve (x + 1)/(x − 2) > 0.', 'Critical values −1 and 2: x < −1 or x > 2.', 9),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Solve x/(x − 1) ≤ 2.', '(x − 2(x − 1))/(x − 1) ≤ 0 → (2 − x)/(x − 1) ≤ 0, so x < 1 or x ≥ 2.', 10),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Why can''t you multiply both sides of an inequality by (x − 1)?', 'Its sign is unknown; multiply by (x − 1)² instead, or use a sign diagram.', 11),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the equation of a parabola in standard form?', 'y² = 4ax, with focus (a, 0) and directrix x = −a.', 12),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the equation of an ellipse centred at the origin?', 'x²/a² + y²/b² = 1.', 13),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the equation of a hyperbola centred at the origin?', 'x²/a² − y²/b² = 1, with asymptotes y = ±(b/a)x.', 14),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is a rectangular hyperbola?', 'xy = c², with the axes as asymptotes.', 15),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What are the parametric equations of y² = 4ax?', 'x = at², y = 2at.', 16),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What are the parametric equations of an ellipse?', 'x = a cos θ, y = b sin θ.', 17),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What are the parametric equations of xy = c²?', 'x = ct, y = c/t.', 18),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the effect of replacing x with x − a in a curve''s equation?', 'A translation by a in the x-direction.', 19),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the effect of replacing y with y/b?', 'A stretch parallel to the y-axis, scale factor b.', 20),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you find stationary points of y = (x² − 3)/(x − 2) without calculus?', 'Rearrange as a quadratic in x with parameter y, and find where the discriminant is zero.', 21),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is a partial fraction decomposition used for in further algebra?', 'Summing series (method of differences) and integration.', 22),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Sketch key features of y = 1/(x² − 1).', 'Vertical asymptotes at x = ±1, horizontal asymptote y = 0, y-intercept −1, symmetric about the y-axis.', 23),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What does a modulus inequality |x − 3| < 2x require?', 'Consider both cases or square carefully (only valid when both sides are non-negative); solution x > 1.', 24),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the discriminant condition for a line to meet a conic?', 'Substitute to get a quadratic; ≥ 0 means the line meets the curve, = 0 means tangent.', 25),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Find the asymptotes of y = (2x − 1)/(x + 3).', 'x = −3 and y = 2.', 26),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What happens to y = 1/f(x) where f(x) = 1?', 'The graphs intersect, since 1/1 = 1.', 27),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What happens to y = 1/f(x) as f(x) → ∞?', 'It tends to 0.', 28),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you sketch y = f(|x|)?', 'Reflect the part for x ≥ 0 in the y-axis (the left part is replaced).', 29),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the focus–directrix property of a parabola?', 'Every point is equidistant from the focus and the directrix.', 30),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is Σ r from r = 1 to n?', 'n(n + 1)/2.', 1),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is Σ r² from r = 1 to n?', 'n(n + 1)(2n + 1)/6.', 2),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is Σ r³ from r = 1 to n?', 'n²(n + 1)²/4.', 3),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is Σ 1 from r = 1 to n?', 'n.', 4),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Evaluate Σ r² from r = 1 to 10.', '10 × 11 × 21/6 = 385.', 5),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find Σ (2r − 1) from r = 1 to n.', 'n(n + 1) − n = n².', 6),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find Σ r(r + 1) from r = 1 to n.', 'Σr² + Σr = n(n + 1)(n + 2)/3.', 7),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'How do you evaluate Σ from r = 11 to 20?', 'Σ from 1 to 20 minus Σ from 1 to 10.', 8),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the method of differences?', 'Writing each term as f(r) − f(r + 1) so that most terms cancel when summed.', 9),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Use the method of differences to sum Σ 1/(r(r + 1)).', '1/(r(r + 1)) = 1/r − 1/(r + 1), so the sum from 1 to n is 1 − 1/(n + 1).', 10),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find Σ 1/(r(r + 2)) from r = 1 to n.', '½ Σ (1/r − 1/(r + 2)) = ½(3/2 − 1/(n + 1) − 1/(n + 2)).', 11),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is a telescoping series?', 'A series in which consecutive terms cancel, leaving only a few terms.', 12),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the sum to infinity of Σ 1/(r(r + 1))?', '1.', 13),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'How do you prove a summation formula?', 'Using the standard results, the method of differences, or proof by induction.', 14),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is Σ (ar + b)?', 'aΣr + bn.', 15),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is a Maclaurin series?', 'f(x) = f(0) + f''(0)x + f''''(0)x²/2! + f''''''(0)x³/3! + …', 16),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the Maclaurin series for eˣ?', '1 + x + x²/2! + x³/3! + …, valid for all x.', 17),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the Maclaurin series for sin x?', 'x − x³/3! + x⁵/5! − …, valid for all x.', 18),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the Maclaurin series for cos x?', '1 − x²/2! + x⁴/4! − …, valid for all x.', 19),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the Maclaurin series for ln(1 + x)?', 'x − x²/2 + x³/3 − …, valid for −1 < x ≤ 1.', 20),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the Maclaurin series for (1 + x)ⁿ?', '1 + nx + n(n − 1)x²/2! + …, valid for |x| < 1 (non-integer n).', 21),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find the Maclaurin series for e^(2x) up to x³.', '1 + 2x + 2x² + (4/3)x³.', 22),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find the series for sin 3x up to x³.', '3x − (27/6)x³ = 3x − 4.5x³.', 23),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find the series for eˣ sin x up to x³.', '(1 + x + x²/2)(x − x³/6) = x + x² + x³/3 + …', 24),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find the series for ln(1 − x) up to x³.', '−x − x²/2 − x³/3.', 25),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'What is the validity of ln(1 − x)''s series?', '−1 ≤ x < 1.', 26),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'How can a Maclaurin series approximate a value?', 'Substitute a small x into the first few terms, e.g. e^0.1 ≈ 1 + 0.1 + 0.005.', 27),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'How can series find limits?', 'Replace functions with their series and simplify, e.g. lim (sin x)/x = 1.', 28),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find lim (x→0) of (1 − cos x)/x².', '(x²/2 − …)/x² → 1/2.', 29),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Series', 'Find lim (x→0) of (eˣ − 1)/x.', '(x + x²/2 + …)/x → 1.', 30),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'What is an improper integral?', 'An integral where a limit is infinite or the integrand is undefined at a point in the range.', 1),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'How do you evaluate ∫₁^∞ 1/x² dx?', 'lim (t→∞) [−1/x]₁ᵗ = 1.', 2),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'Does ∫₁^∞ 1/x dx converge?', 'No; ln t → ∞, so it diverges.', 3),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'Evaluate ∫₀¹ 1/√x dx.', '[2√x]₀¹ = 2 (the integral converges even though 1/√x is undefined at 0).', 4),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'What is the mean value of f(x) over [a, b]?', '(1/(b − a)) ∫ₐᵇ f(x) dx.', 5),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'Find the mean value of x² over [0, 3].', '(1/3) × 9 = 3.', 6),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Further Calculus', 'What is ∫ 1/√(1 − x²) dx?', 'arcsin x + c.', 7),
